after:
Run this example in a fresh database:
```sql
CREATE TABLE demo_readings (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  value INTEGER NOT NULL
) STRICT;
INSERT INTO demo_readings VALUES (1, '12'), (2, '06');
SELECT id, value, typeof(value) AS kind
FROM demo_readings
ORDER BY id;
```
The values are `12` and `6`. Both have kind `integer`.
